## 10. Full Input Parameters Reference

### General Settings
- **History**: Number of historical setups to render on chart.
- **Visible Only**: When ON, only setups belonging to visible HTF candles are rendered.
- **Fractal Mode**:
  - `Automatic`: Uses standard higher-timeframe alignment (e.g. 1m $\rightarrow$ 15m, 5m $\rightarrow$ 1H, 15m $\rightarrow$ 4H, 1H $\rightarrow$ 1D).
  - `Quarterly`: Activates ICT Quarterly Theory session modes (`SESSION_MICRO`, `SESSION_90`, `SESSION_6H`).
  - `Custom`: Enter any user-defined LTF/HTF pair.
- **Bias**: `Neutral`, `Bullish`, or `Bearish` filter.

### SMT Divergence Settings
- **SMT Mode**: `Automatic` (auto-routes correlated pairs) or `Manual`.
- **Enable Second / Third SMT**: Toggles 3-way correlation matrix.
- **SMT Line Style / Width / Color**: Customize divergence rendering.

### Side-by-Side HTF Settings (HTF 2, 3, 4)
- **Show Second / Third / Fourth HTF**: Toggle display of extra timeframes.
- **Timeframe**: Set desired HTF (e.g. `240` for 4H, `D` for Daily, `W` for Weekly).
- **Candles**: Number of candles to display (1 to 20).
- **Gap**: Horizontal spacing in bars between sets.
- **Vertical Lines**: Toggle session separators on LTF chart.

### Performance Settings
- **Calculate on Close**: When enabled, live setup detection only runs on candle close (improves execution speed).
- **Calculation Lookback**: Limits historical scan depth (default: 1,500 bars) for instantaneous chart loading.

